  "notes": "The purple-tape palette, and the parameter nothing else on this axis has is the scale table: the research names melodic-minor and harmonic-minor motifs specifically, so `melodic_minor` sits at real weight rather than as a colour — that raised 6th and 7th over a minor tonic is the cinematic string sound the entry describes. The other identifying claim is negative space: \"Long silences between motif statements\" and \"heavy use of loop-only bars with drums muted\", authored as `melody.densityPerBar` 1–4 and `arrangement.transitions.dropOutBeats.prob` 0.8, the highest in this batch. Hats are sparse, so the hat block is non-continuous; `fillDensity` is held at 0.3 because a model that declares a hat block owes every seed a hat. `timbreHint` is `piano` for the solo piano or violin figure, and there are no pads, which is why the countermelody is an answer lick rather than an `arp` wash. ⚠ **The bass is `mirror_kick`, not a held note, and that is an engine limit rather than a reading of the record.** The research says sustained sub on the tonic with an occasional two-note motion; `followRootsProb` 0.9 with `P5` as the only passing tone is that two-note motion, and `reese_sustain` is refused because it saturates. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium; the album production and RZA's method are documented but the tempo band is catalog-level.",
